# ==========================================================================
#  PE6201 individual project — what is deliberately NOT committed
#  Everything excluded here is either secret, third-party, or regenerable.
# ==========================================================================

# --- 1. secrets: never commit -------------------------------------------
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
!**/.env.example
**/server_token.txt
**/*_token.txt

# --- 2. the instructor's own course material (not our work) --------------
study slides/

# --- 3. local agent / editor state ---------------------------------------
.workbuddy/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- 4. python ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- 5. node / vite -------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.vite/
*.timestamp-*.mjs

# --- 6. rebuildable indexes and derived artefacts -------------------------
#   Regenerated by the commands in README.md §6 "Reproducing".
#   NOTE: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory,
#   so the `**/` prefix is required — without it these would not match
#   `resume_jd_matcher/artifacts/...` at all.
**/chroma_db/
**/server_index/
**/kb_index/
**/tmp_run/

# --- 7. logs, scratch, OS cruft ------------------------------------------
*.log
*.bak
*.tmp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.lnk

# --- 8. demo video --------------------------------------------------------
#   No video is committed.  The raw capture is 167 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB
#   per-file hard limit; the 17.6 MB re-encode is not committed either, because
#   this repository is public and the presenter is on camera throughout.
#   The video ships on NTULearn — see README.md §0 row 2 and §2.
demo_video.mp4
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov

# --- 9. the author's process archive — untracked, still on local disk ------
#   These files built the deliverables: report patch scripts, the extracted
#   text of the instructor's decks, the Chinese report mirror, the superseded
#   report drafts, the probe scripts.  They are deliberately NOT part of the
#   submission, but they are also NOT deleted from this machine — so
#   `scripts/check_no_chinese.py` still sees them locally and still covers
#   them with the exceptions it declares.  Rules below stop them coming back
#   on the next `git add -A`; already-tracked files ignore them.
/report/slides_text/
/report/feedback.txt
/report/report_zh.md
/report/_patch_*.py
/report/_verify_v[1-7]_quotes.py
/report/_verify_addendum_quotes.py
/report/_verify_business_quotes.py
/report/_verify_refined_quotes.py
/report/_verify_report.py
/report/_diag*.py
/report/_extract_a1_files.py
/report/_fetch_esco.py
/report/_append_memory_10.py
/report/_[a-z]*.txt
/report/_[a-z]*.json
/report/final_report_v[1-7]*
/report/writeup_material_*.md
/report/material_for_writeup.md
/report/requirement_traceability.md
/report/PE6201_Project_Problem_Statement*.txt
/_[a-z]*.py
/_*.txt
/resume_jd_matcher/_*.py
/resume_jd_matcher/_*.md
/resume_jd_matcher/_*.txt
/resume_jd_matcher/artifacts_preflight/
/resume_jd_matcher/src/llm/app.py
